# ADDITIVE REFERENCE ONLY. Keep the existing production .env, MongoDB database,
# JWT_SECRET, storage, mail/messaging values and other operational settings.
# Do not copy this template over a working production environment.

# Preferred protection for saved Admin API keys. Generate ONCE, store securely
# and back up with MongoDB; losing/changing it locks saved credentials.
# python -c 'from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())'
API_SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# A strong, explicit, stable existing JWT_SECRET may supply the compatibility
# derivation only when the dedicated key is absent. Never rotate it casually.
# Keep your existing JWT_SECRET; no replacement/sample secret is supplied here.

# Existing runtime defaults remain Emergent for both purposes. Preserve the
# actual existing EMERGENT_LLM_KEY securely; this file contains no provider key.
# AI_TEXT_PROVIDER=emergent
# AI_IMAGE_PROVIDER=emergent
# AI_TEXT_MODEL=gemini-3-flash-preview
# AI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview
# EMERGENT_LLM_KEY=

# Direct Google is OPTIONAL and requires an explicit matching provider choice.
# A Google key by itself never switches the existing Emergent defaults.
# AI_TEXT_PROVIDER=google
# AI_IMAGE_PROVIDER=google
# AI_TEXT_MODEL=gemini-3-flash-preview
# AI_IMAGE_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-image
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# Optional image-specific Google key overrides the shared Google key:
# GEMINI_IMAGE_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_IMAGE_API_KEY=

# Admin saves apply per generation without restart. Blank key inputs keep a
# saved override; explicit clear removes that override but ENV fallback remains.
# Saving/loading makes no provider request; explicit Test has documented limits.
# See deploy/DEPLOY.md, Encrypted Admin API Settings, before using production.
